Steve Leferve wrote:
>
> I typically abstain from
> inventory management -- I like to go through several floors, explore, and
> get in fights. It seems to me, however, that better players will clear a
> floor, collect everything, indentify, store, move boxes and chests, and
> *then* go to the next level. How boring! Is this what it takes to be a good
> player?

Some amount of inventory management is needed to survive.  Some
amount of building a stash is needed to have ascension quality
equipment.  Do neither and forget ascension.  Moving every item
from every floor to your stash is excessive for a quick ascension,
but if you want a sure thing it works.  Find a tradeoff between
the two extremes.

Some stash on each level, some keep a stash and never move it
to other levels.  Few who decline to stash survive the depths,
but no-stash would be a fun challenge.

